assert len(S) == 44
takeaways = [
 '**Distributed organization:** Cassiopea has stage-specific neural and muscular architectures; detailed motor- and diffuse-net maps from Aurelia provide comparative evidence rather than a complete Cassiopea circuit.',
 '**Localized rhythmic drive:** Isolated rhopalia retain electrical activity, and rhopalia removal permits externally controlled contractions, separating endogenous initiation from preserved motor capacity.',
 '**Generation and propagation:** A pacemaker can initiate repeated activity, whereas a closed conducting path can sustain reentry; repeated bell movement alone does not distinguish these mechanisms.',
 '**Bounded molecular causation:** Nicotine, tubocurarine and chrnal-E RNAi connect receptor-related mechanisms to rhythm and behavioral state, without establishing an endogenous acetylcholine transmitter pathway.',
 '**State-dependent output:** Day–night pulse changes, reversible arousal delays and compensatory quiescence support regulated sleep-like behavior rather than simple muscle failure.',
 '**Recovery with altered anatomy:** Rhopalia influence regeneration, and halved ephyrae regain pulsing and feeding with fewer marginal organs; functional recovery does not imply restoration of every original connection.'
]
